From b96fde656a352527208a2020dc089c6773df3c2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Urho Laurinen <urho.laurinen@siroic.com>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 10/12] gptel: Let pre-tool-call hook errors propagate

`gptel-pre-tool-call-functions' are gatekeepers: a hook may return
:stop to abort the request before a tool runs.  Wrapping the call in
`with-demoted-errors' means a hook that fails -- including one that fails
while deciding to stop the request -- is merely logged, and the tool then
runs as if the hook had approved it.  That turns a policy or safety hook
into a no-op precisely when it is most important, and the message is
easy to miss mid-response.

Drop the `with-demoted-errors' wrapper so such errors surface through the
normal request error path.  This is deliberately a behaviour change: a
buggy hook now fails loudly rather than being ignored.

No test: the change removes error demotion, so the only observable difference is that an error propagates instead of being logged -- a property of the surrounding request error path, not of a unit under test.
---
diff --git a/gptel.el b/gptel.el
index 16110c4..050b603 100644
--- a/gptel.el
+++ b/gptel.el
@@ -1507,9 +1507,12 @@ Perform UI updates and run post-response hooks."
                  (let* ((name (plist-get tool-call :name))
                         (args (plist-get tool-call :args))
                         (hook-func-result
-                         (with-demoted-errors "gptel-pre-tool-call hook error: %S"
-                           (funcall hook-func (nconc (list :name name :args args)
-                                                     hook-func-args)))))
+                         ;; Do not demote errors here: `gptel-pre-tool-call-functions'
+                         ;; are gatekeepers that may stop the request, so a genuine
+                         ;; failure in one must propagate instead of being silently
+                         ;; logged and the tool run anyway.
+                         (funcall hook-func (nconc (list :name name :args args)
+                                                   hook-func-args))))
                    (if (plist-get hook-func-result :stop) ; Stop the request immediately
                        (let ((reason (or (plist-get hook-func-result :stop-reason)
                                          (concat "Request stopped by pre-tool-call hook "
